# JS systems

## Style

- ESM (`"type": "module"`). Plain JS with JSDoc `@param` / `@type` — no TypeScript.
- File header comment stating what the module owns and any load-bearing order.
- Import Babylon from deep paths (`@babylonjs/core/...`), not the barrel package.
- Classes own construction + `update(dt, …)` + optional `async warmUp()` / `setVisible` / `registerPrepass`.

## Settings

- Tunables live on flat `S` in `core/settings.js` (read every frame; no proxies).
- Overlay widgets come from `SCHEMA` (`t: "f"|"b"|"e"`). Add both `S` key and SCHEMA entry together.
- Use `onChange(key, fn)` only when an edit needs rebuild work; otherwise sample `S` next frame.
- Writes go through `set(k, v)` — never from the render loop.

## GPU / materials

- `ShaderLanguage.WGSL` on every `ShaderMaterial` / `ProceduralTexture`.
- Shader names must match `shaders/registry.js` (`snow`, `wake`, `water`, … → `*VertexShader` / `*PixelShader`).
- Prefer `bindMatrixArray` over `setMatrices` for per-frame cascade uploads (avoids GC).
- Shadow casters register their **actual** depth vertex program via `ShadowSystem.registerCaster` — Babylon's stock cascades cannot see procedural geometry.
- Opaque casters that feed post also `registerPrepass` on `DepthPass`.

## Frame wiring

Call order in `main.js` is intentional (contact after figure pose; spells before `terrain.update` so brushes land; wake before spray upload). Preserve or update comments when changing order.
